KNOWNBUG
main.cpp
--cpp17
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ decltype\(auto\) over std::get pack: 1\+2==3: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ WRONG must FAIL: FAILURE$
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
--
KNOWNBUG: a function template with a DEDUCED return type (decltype(auto)) whose
body expands a pack of REAL std::get calls, `return add(std::get<I>(t)...)` --
the shape of libstdc++ std::apply's __apply_impl
(`std::__invoke(f, std::get<_Idx>(t)...)`).  CBMC fails to deduce the return type
("could not fully type-check 'main'"); the body is left incomplete so both
assertions are skipped -> VERIFICATION SUCCESSFUL vacuously, which does NOT match
the desc above (so a known bug).  Hand-written stand-ins for std::get are handled
(cpp17_nested_decltype_auto_pack_call, CORE); the defect is specific to the real
std::get, whose overloaded / tuple_element-based return type must be resolved for
each pack element inside the enclosing decltype(auto) deduction.  This is the
remaining cpp17_apply_basic blocker (there it surfaces as the unresolved
`<<type:decltype>>` return type of std::apply).  The tuple is by reference, so
this is independent of the separate std::get-by-value-copy value bug.  g++ runs
r == 3; clang++ accepts.  When fixed, assertion 2 fails and the desc matches.
